{
	quest.B1000000000002BC.title: "Yellorium"
	quest.B1000000000002BC.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Fuel"
	quest.B1000000000002BC.quest_desc: [
		"Extreme Reactors turns yellorium into FE — first as a small passive reactor, then as an actively cooled steam loop into a turbine. This chapter walks you from ore to ludicrite endgame.",
		"",
		"&6You will:&r\n&e•&r Mine yellorite and stock graphite for reactor parts\n&e•&r Build a hollow Basic reactor with fuel rods, control rods, and a power tap\n&e•&r Graduate to active cooling, turbines, cyanite reprocessing, and Reinforced tier",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Start tiny. A 5×5×5 outer shell (~3×3×3 interior) teaches the layout before you scale.",
		"",
		"&6Goal:&r Smelt &616 Yellorium Ingots&r.",
		"",
		"Yellorium is the fuel metal every Basic reactor burns. Without a stockpile, your first controller is just a fancy doorstop.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Hunt &6Yellorite Ore&r underground (deepslate variants count). Nature's Compass won't find it — dig, explore, or filter a Digital Miner.\n&e2.&r Smelt the ore into &eYellorium Ingots&r and keep extras for fuel rods plus later crafts.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Batch-smelt; inserting fuel and crafting parts both chew through ingots.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Graphite next — casings and rods need it in bulk.",
		"",
		"&6Connected:&r",
		"{\"text\":\"\\u2192 Alternator\",\"color\":\"yellow\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"B10000000000019B\"}}"
	]
	quest.B1000000000002BD.title: "Graphite Bars"
	quest.B1000000000002BD.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Materials"
	quest.B1000000000002BD.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &616 Graphite Bars&r.",
		"",
		"Graphite shows up in casings, fuel rods, control rods, and turbine parts. Treat it like a second fuel supply for the whole chapter.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Open JEI for &6Graphite Bar&r — charcoal, coal coke, or similar carbon routes depending on the pack.\n&e2.&r Craft a chestful and park it next to your reactor build site.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Running out mid-shell is painful; overshoot on the first batch.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Casings form the hollow reactor shell."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002BE.title: "Reactor Casing"
	quest.B1000000000002BE.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Reactor"
	quest.B1000000000002BE.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &624 Basic Reactor Casings&r.",
		"",
		"Casings (and glass) make the hollow cuboid shell. Controllers, ports, and taps replace face blocks later — corners must always stay casing.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Pick a starter footprint: outer &e5×5×5&r (about &e3×3×3&r interior) is ideal. Basic reactors top out near &e5×5×5&r interior — don't max it on day one.\n&e2.&r Build a hollow cuboid: floor, walls, and ceiling of &6Basic Reactor Casing&r. Leave the interior empty air.\n&e3.&r Corners and edges must be casing. You can swap some wall faces for reactor glass once you craft it — never the corners.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Frame the shell first, then punch holes for the controller, power tap, and access port.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r The controller validates the multiblock."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002BF.title: "Reactor Controller"
	quest.B1000000000002BF.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Reactor"
	quest.B1000000000002BF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Basic Reactor Controller.",
		"",
		"The controller is the brain — it assembles the multiblock and shows heat, fuel, reactivity, and power. No valid controller, no reactor.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Replace one face block (not a corner) with the &6Basic Reactor Controller&r.\n&e2.&r Stand back and confirm the structure assembles (outline / GUI). If it fails, check hollow interior, casing corners, and that only valid reactor parts sit on the shell.\n&e3.&r Leave room on other faces for a &ePower Tap&r and &eAccess Port&r — don't cover every wall with glass yet.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Controller on the front face, ports on the sides keeps cable runs tidy.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Fuel rods go in interior columns under control rods."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002C0.title: "Fuel Rods"
	quest.B1000000000002C0.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Reactor"
	quest.B1000000000002C0.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &64 Basic Reactor Fuel Rods&r.",
		"",
		"Fuel rods hold yellorium inside the hollow core. Each column of rods is one fuel channel — more rods means more heat and power, and more waste.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Inside the hollow volume, place vertical columns of &6Basic Reactor Fuel Rods&r from floor level up toward the ceiling.\n&e2.&r Start with one or two short columns — four rods is plenty for a first reactor.\n&e3.&r Leave the block directly above each column free for a &eControl Rod&r (next quest).",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Don't pack the entire interior on the first build; learn heat before you scale.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Control rods sit on top of each fuel column."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002C1.title: "Control Rods"
	quest.B1000000000002C1.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Reactor"
	quest.B1000000000002C1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &62 Basic Reactor Control Rods&r.",
		"",
		"Control rods cap each fuel column and let you throttle reactivity from the controller GUI. Insertion high = cooler, safer startup.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place a &6Basic Reactor Control Rod&r in the ceiling / top face directly above each fuel-rod column.\n&e2.&r Confirm every fuel column has a matching control rod — orphan rods won't moderate properly.\n&e3.&r Before inserting fuel, set insertion high (nearly fully inserted) so the first light-off stays gentle.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Always throttle with rods before you add more fuel rods later.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r A passive power tap pulls FE without a turbine."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002C2.title: "Power Tap"
	quest.B1000000000002C2.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Reactor"
	quest.B1000000000002C2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Basic Passive FE Power Tap.",
		"",
		"Passive cooling dumps heat as FE through a power tap — the simplest Extreme Reactors setup. Active cooling (steam out → turbine) comes later for much higher output.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Replace a face casing (not a corner) with the &6Passive FE Power Tap&r.\n&e2.&r Connect energy cables / conduits from the tap to a battery or your factory bus.\n&e3.&r Insert yellorium through an access port (next) or by hand, then slowly withdraw control rods while watching heat in the controller.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r If heat climbs faster than your cables can drain, push rods back in before you expand.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Access ports automate fuel in and cyanite out."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002C3.title: "Access Port"
	quest.B1000000000002C3.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Reactor"
	quest.B1000000000002C3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Basic Solid Access Port.",
		"",
		"The solid access port is how yellorium enters and cyanite waste leaves. Automate it early so you aren't hand-feeding a hot core.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Replace another face block with the &6Basic Solid Access Port&r.\n&e2.&r Configure the port for fuel input / waste output, then pipe yellorium in and cyanite out with item pipes or transporters.\n&e3.&r With port, tap, controller, fuel columns, and control rods in place, light the reactor and confirm FE on the tap.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Cyanite stacks up fast — chest it or send it toward the reprocessor branch.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Two paths open: collect cyanite, or start the turbine line for active cooling."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002C4.title: "Cyanite Waste"
	quest.B1000000000002C4.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Fuel cycle"
	quest.B1000000000002C4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Collect &68 Cyanite Ingots&r.",
		"",
		"Burned yellorium becomes cyanite. It's not trash — reprocessing turns waste into the next fuel tier toward blutonium and ludicrite.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Run the reactor until spent fuel ejects as &6Cyanite&r through the access port.\n&e2.&r Pull eight ingots into your inventory (or a chest the quest can see).\n&e3.&r Stockpile the rest; the reprocessor will want a steady feed.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Don't void cyanite if you care about the endgame fuel ladder.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Craft the reprocessor controller when you're ready to recycle."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002C5.title: "Turbine Housing"
	quest.B1000000000002C5.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Turbine"
	quest.B1000000000002C5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &620 Basic Turbine Housings&r.",
		"",
		"Active cooling vents steam from the reactor into a turbine multiblock. Steam → rotor → coils makes far more FE than a passive power tap alone.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Build a hollow turbine shell from &6Basic Turbine Housing&r — leave room for a central rotor shaft, blades, coils, and a bearing.\n&e2.&r Plan fluid ports: steam in from the reactor (or a steam buffer), water/condensate out.\n&e3.&r Keep the turbine near the reactor so steam pipes stay short.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Switch the reactor to active cooling only after the turbine shell and ports are ready.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r The turbine controller assembles the multiblock."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002C6.title: "Turbine Controller"
	quest.B1000000000002C6.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Turbine"
	quest.B1000000000002C6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Basic Turbine Controller.",
		"",
		"The controller validates the turbine and exposes RPM, steam intake, and energy output. Tune coil and blade counts from here.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place the &6Basic Turbine Controller&r on a housing face (not a corner).\n&e2.&r Add a rotor bearing, a straight &eRotor Shaft&r down the axis, and leave space for blades and inductive coils around/along the design JEI shows.\n&e3.&r Mount fluid ports for steam intake and water exhaust, plus a power tap for FE out.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Match blades and coils to your steam supply — overspeed or under-coiled rotors waste efficiency.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Rotor blades catch the steam flow."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002C7.title: "Rotor Blades"
	quest.B1000000000002C7.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Turbine"
	quest.B1000000000002C7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &68 Basic Turbine Rotor Blades&r.",
		"",
		"Blades on the rotor convert steam flow into shaft RPM. Coils then turn that spin into FE — balance both sides of the machine.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Attach &6Rotor Blades&r along the shaft per the turbine layout (pairs of blades on shaft segments).\n&e2.&r Install inductive coils in their designated coil region so RPM produces energy instead of free-spinning.\n&e3.&r Feed steam, watch RPM in the controller, and adjust blade/coil count if intake and induction don't match.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Too many blades without coils stalls; too many coils without blades underproduce.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Meanwhile, recycle cyanite in the reprocessor."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002C8.title: "Cyanite Reprocessor"
	quest.B1000000000002C8.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Fuel cycle"
	quest.B1000000000002C8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Reprocessor Controller.",
		"",
		"The cyanite reprocessor multiblock turns waste back into useful fuel feedstocks for the next tier — required if you want blutonium and ludicrite.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Build the reprocessor shell from its casings (JEI / Patchouli list every part).\n&e2.&r Place the &6Collector&r on the bottom center and the &6Waste Injector&r on the top center.\n&e3.&r Put power, fluid, and output ports on the sides; pipe cyanite into the injector and pull products from the output.\n&e4.&r Power the machine and run a small cyanite batch to confirm the loop before you scale the reactor.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Keep a buffer chest between the reactor access port and the waste injector.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Reinforced parts unlock larger, hotter cores."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002C9.title: "Reinforced Reactor"
	quest.B1000000000002C9.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Endgame"
	quest.B1000000000002C9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Reinforced Reactor Controller.",
		"",
		"Reinforced reactors dwarf Basic size limits, handle hotter fuels, and pair with serious turbine loops. Upgrade when Basic heat or footprint is the bottleneck — not before cyanite recycling is stable.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Craft the &6Reinforced Reactor Controller&r and matching reinforced casings / rods as JEI shows.\n&e2.&r Build a larger hollow cuboid the same way: casing corners, hollow interior, fuel columns with control rods on top, ports on faces.\n&e3.&r Move to active cooling + turbine if you haven't already — Reinforced output will swamp a lone passive tap.",
		"",
		"&cCaution:&r Bigger cores melt faster when cooling or rod control lags. Commission cool before you fill every fuel column.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Migrate your access-port automation and waste line before the first Reinforced light-off.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Ludicrite is the bragging-rights endgame metal."
	]
	quest.B1000000000002CA.title: "Ludicrite"
	quest.B1000000000002CA.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Reactors · Endgame"
	quest.B1000000000002CA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &64 Ludicrite Ingots&r.",
		"",
		"Ludicrite is Extreme Reactors' endgame material — top-tier components and proof your fuel cycle (cyanite → blutonium → ludicrite) actually works.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Follow JEI for &6Ludicrite&r — blutonium from reprocessing plus End-dimension or other gated ingredients typically appear.\n&e2.&r Keep the reprocessor fed so blutonium doesn't become the bottleneck mid-craft.\n&e3.&r Craft four ingots and stash spares for any ludicrite-tier parts you still want.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r If a ingredient looks alien, check the End and your cyanite stocks first."
	]
}
